# shellcheck baseline for automation/
#
# Established by DRAFT-031. The point of this file is that the *bare*
# command exits 0 against unmodified working code:
#
#     shellcheck automation/*.sh          # picks this file up automatically
#
# Bare, because that is what `CLAUDE.md`, `README.md` and
# `docs/workflow-ci.md` all tell a developer and the CI tier (DRAFT-026a)
# to run. A gate that is red by default gets ignored, and one that only
# passes with flags nobody remembers is the same gate.
#
# Nothing here is suppressed without naming the issue that removes it.
# A suppression with no owner is not an exception, it is an untracked
# defect. When an owning issue lands, delete its line.

# --- Why `disable=` and not a severity floor ----------------------------
#
# The natural expression of this policy is `severity=warning`: every
# finding below is `info` or `style`, and `shellcheck -S warning
# automation/*.sh` does exit 0 today. It is not used because
# **`severity=` in this file is silently ignored by shellcheck 0.11.0** --
# measured, not assumed: an rc containing only `severity=warning` changes
# neither the output nor the exit status, while `disable=` in the same
# file works. Only the CLI `-S` flag applies a floor.
#
# So the choice was between a bare command that passes (this file) and a
# documented flag that everyone must remember (`-S warning`). This file
# wins, at a cost stated plainly below.
#
# Re-test `severity=` when shellcheck is upgraded. If it starts working it
# is strictly better than the blanket disables here, because it keeps the
# checks live for code written after this baseline.

# --- Dialect ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# No `shell=` override, deliberately. Each file's own shebang is the
# authority, so a new per-OS script cannot be silently checked as a dialect
# it does not run under.
#
# The five DRAKVUF-derived worker scripts declare `#!/bin/sh` and are
# checked as POSIX sh, which is what actually interprets them: `dirwatch`
# spawns them via `g_spawn_command_line_sync()` and `/bin/sh` is `dash` on
# the Dom0 host. `run_analysis-ubuntu.sh` declares `#!/bin/bash` and is
# checked as bash, because it is this project's own launcher, invoked
# directly by an operator rather than by `dirwatch`.

# --- Accepted findings --------------------------------------------------
#
# SC1091  Not following: pipeline-ubuntu.env was not specified as input.
#         Correct behaviour, not a defect: the config is sourced at runtime
#         from a path built at runtime. The `# shellcheck source=`
#         directives in the scripts record where it lives.
#         Owner: none needed.
#
# SC2086  Unquoted expansions, 33 sites across cleanup.sh,
#         drakvuf-ubuntu.sh, network-setup.sh, tcpdump.sh.
#         Owner: DRAFT-030 (guest-filename normalizer) and DRAFT-011.
#         NOT fixed here on purpose -- changing expansion behaviour in
#         scripts that run malware analysis as root is a behaviour change
#         and goes through its own review, not a lint cleanup.
#
# SC2009  `ps aux | grep` process discovery, 4 sites. Three are in shared
#         cleanup.sh. The `"tcpdump -i xenbr1.$VLAN"` match is unanchored
#         with `.` as a regex wildcard, so VLAN 1 also matches
#         xenbr1.10-19 once there are more than 9 clones.
#         Owner: DRAFT-011.
#
# SC2006  RETIRED 2026-08-11 by DRAFT-028. Its only site in the repository
#         was network-setup.sh's `for i in \`seq 1 $1\``, replaced by a
#         POSIX while-loop. The check is live again for every file.
#         This is the mechanism working as intended: a suppression named
#         its owning issue, that issue landed, and the line came out.
#
# THE COST, stated because it is not obvious: the remaining two are
# disabled repository-wide, so a genuinely dangerous new unquoted expansion
# in `preconfig-android.sh` or a future `clone-windows.pl` wrapper will NOT
# be caught until DRAFT-030/011 land and these lines come out. That is an
# argument for landing DRAFT-030 sooner rather than a reason to accept the
# disables indefinitely.
#
# For reference, `shellcheck --norc automation/network-setup.sh` is clean
# as of DRAFT-028 -- that file needs none of the exemptions below.
disable=SC1091,SC2086,SC2009